## Phase 2: Identity & Cloud Sync
**Goal:** Secure the app and backup data to the user's own Google Drive.
**Focus:** Kinde Auth + Google Drive REST API.

### Manual Setup (Prerequisites)
1. **Kinde:** Create a project, enable "Google" as a social connection. Add your `duebly.app` URLs to the callback list.
2. **Google Cloud Console:** - Create an OAuth 2.0 Client ID. 
   - Add the scope: `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.appdata` (This lets you save the hidden `todo.json`).
3. **Env Variables:** Add `KINDE_CLIENT_ID`, `KINDE_DOMAIN`, and Google Client IDs to your Cloudflare Pages environment.

### The "One-Shot" Prompt for Phase 2
> "Integrate Kinde Auth and Google Drive Sync into the existing Duebly app.
> 
> **Requirements:**
> 1. Wrap the entire app in a Kinde Auth check. Only logged-in users can access the list.
> 2. Create a `SyncService`: 
>    - On login, check the Google Drive 'App Data' folder for `duebly_backup.json`.
>    - If the cloud version is newer (check `updatedAt` timestamps), update Dexie.js.
>    - On every change in Dexie, debounce a 3-second upload of the full JSON to the Google Drive App Data folder.
> 3. UI: Add a small 'Syncing' indicator and a 'User Profile/Logout' button in the header."

